From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 02:06:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ether: enable the memory and blkio cgroup controllers

Android 13's libprocessgroup mounts both during early init:

  libprocessgroup: Failed to mount blkio cgroup: No such file or directory
  libprocessgroup: Failed to mount memory cgroup: No such file or directory

Neither controller was in the defconfig -- 18.1 never needed them. Both have
existed since well before 3.10, so this is a config gap rather than a kernel
limitation, unlike the cgroup v2 problem in the same log.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig
index 7dcc237a315..0201c01bed0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_ether_defconfig
@@ -12,6 +12,13 @@ CONFIG_RCU_NOCB_CPU_ALL=y
 CONFIG_IKCONFIG=y
 CONFIG_CGROUPS=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_FREEZER=y
+# Android 13 libprocessgroup mounts blkio and memory cgroups during early init. Without these
+# it logs "Failed to mount blkio cgroup" / "Failed to mount memory cgroup" and cannot set up
+# the process groups ueventd and apexd-bootstrap depend on. Both controllers exist in 3.10;
+# they were simply never enabled here because 18.1 did not need them.
+CONFIG_MEMCG=y
+CONFIG_MEMCG_SWAP=y
+CONFIG_BLK_CGROUP=y
 CONFIG_CPUSETS=y
 CONFIG_CGROUP_CPUACCT=y
 CONFIG_RESOURCE_COUNTERS=y
